  - [1mOnly [38;5;153mrequired[39m objects to an empty value.[0m Every other rule passes on [38;5;153m""[39m, so an optional field carrying [38;5;153m[minLength(3)]
[39m    doesn't light up while it's blank. Without this, every optional field needs conditional wiring at each call site.
  - [1m[38;5;153mrequired[39m trims before testing[0m, so a space-only input counts as empty. No other rule mutates the value.

  The file ends with a dual-export footer: assign [38;5;153mFormValidation[39m on [38;5;153mglobalThis[39m for the page, and [38;5;153mmodule.exports[39m when
  [38;5;153mmodule[39m exists for Node.

  [1m2. Wiring the login form[0m

  [38;5;153mindex.html[39m gets [38;5;153m<script src="src/validation.js"></script>[39m before [38;5;153mapp.js[39m. In [38;5;153mapp.js[39m, the inline [38;5;153mvalidateForm[39m goes away,
  replaced by a declared rule set and a call to the shared [38;5;153mvalidate[39m. Login keeps [1mrequired-only[0m rules — deliberately no
  [38;5;153mminLength[39m on the password, so this change alters no login behavior. The one visible difference: failures now log a
  message per field instead of the single [38;5;153m"Missing required fields"[39m string. Rendering errors into the page stays out of
  scope, per your earlier call.

  [1m3. Error handling[0m

  [38;5;153mvalidate[39m is total — it doesn't throw on unexpected input. A field whose rule entry is a bare function rather than an
  array is accepted; [38;5;153mvalues[39m keys with no rules are ignored.

